window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>I need a new man like I need a hole in the head.</p> <p>The last one almost killed me. Literally.</p> <p>I barely escaped with my life, and when I end up on a ranch in Central Texas, I’m just looking for a place to hide out and recover.</p> <p>But then Reece Walker saunters in.</p> <p><i>(Why, God? Do you enjoy torturing me like this? Is it fun for you?)</i></p> <p>I tell myself it’ll just be one night. We’ll do the horizontal mambo and then I’ll have him out of my system.…</p> <p>But it turns out Reece isn’t the kind of man you easily forget. Especially when I end up staying on at the ranch. Day in, day out, he’s there. Him and his big blue eyes, stupid muscles, dumb jokes, and searing gazes that hit me straight in the - <br> ahem. Nope. Not falling for it. I’ve got way too much baggage and I gotta be moving on soon.</p> <p>I can’t think about building a future when I never know if my past might catch up with me....</p>"; 
